    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Descendants of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donghu">Donghu</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> as masters of the Mongolian steppe after 91 CE.</li><li>Tanshihuai united them around 156 CE and destroyed a major Han expedition into the steppe in 177 CE.</li><li>Their clans, above all the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuoba">Tuoba</a> of the Northern Wei, went on to rule much of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-the-later-han">Hou Han shu</a>, Tanshihuai's mother conceived him after a hailstone fell into her mouth; her husband, away at war for three years, at first refused to raise the child.</p></aside>
    </section>

